  <keyword>ode mass implicit tutorial</keyword>
  <short_description>Solve mass matrix and implicit ODE problems.</short_description>
  <description>
    <p>Use the <b>Mass</b> option when the system is written as <b>M(t,y)y'=f(t,y)</b>. A constant matrix, scalar, or function handle can define the mass matrix.</p>
    <table style="width:100%">
  <tr><th>Problem form</th><th>Entry point</th><th>Required data</th></tr>
  <tr><td><b>M(t,y)y' = f(t,y)</b></td><td><b>ode15s</b>, <b>ode23t</b>, <b>ode23tb</b></td><td><b>Mass</b> option and initial value.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><b>F(t,y,yp) = 0</b></td><td><b>ode15i</b></td><td>Initial value and initial slope.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Object workflow</td><td><b>ode</b> with <b>EquationType</b></td><td>Residual function, initial value, and optional initial slope.</td></tr>
</table>
    <p>Use <b>ode15i</b> for fully implicit residual equations <b>F(t,y,yp)=0</b>. The function form uses the initial value and initial slope that you provide. In the object workflow, <b>ComputeConsistentInitialConditions</b> can adjust the initial slope while keeping the initial value fixed.</p>
  </description>
  <examples>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description>Constant mass matrix.</example_item_description>
      <example_item_data runnable="cli"><![CDATA[options = odeset('Mass', 2, 'Jacobian', 1);
[t, y] = ode15s(@(t,y) y, [0 0.5], 1, options)]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description>Implicit residual equation.</example_item_description>
      <example_item_data runnable="cli"><![CDATA[f = @(t,y,yp) yp + y;
[t, y] = ode15i(f, [0 1], 1, -1)]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
  </examples>
